1
00:00:00,225 --> 00:00:07,275
This is The Vibe Coder's Handbook, a visual guide to commanding AI and modern developers.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,637
Apple doesn't sell websites.

3
00:00:09,637 --> 00:00:11,157
Nike doesn't sell buttons.

4
00:00:11,157 --> 00:00:12,735
Spotify doesn't sell menus.

5
00:00:12,735 --> 00:00:14,021
They sell experiences.

6
00:00:14,021 --> 00:00:17,470
The front end is the stage, where technology meets emotion.

7
00:00:17,470 --> 00:00:23,667
The code is the machinery behind the curtain, and to build experiences, you must understand the machinery.

8
00:00:24,292 --> 00:00:25,497
Chapter one.

9
00:00:25,497 --> 00:00:28,208
How the web actually works.

10
00:00:28,933 --> 00:00:31,166
When you tap an app, it feels instant.

11
00:00:31,166 --> 00:00:35,337
But behind that single tap is a conversation between dozens of systems.

12
00:00:35,337 --> 00:00:44,796
Your request travels from the user, to the device, to the browser, across the internet, to a server, into a database, through code, and back again as a response.

13
00:00:44,796 --> 00:00:47,733
The Vibe Coder understands this invisible journey.

14
00:00:48,883 --> 00:00:50,618
The internet is three things.

15
00:00:50,618 --> 00:00:54,448
The client, the thing asking for information, like your browser.

16
00:00:54,448 --> 00:00:57,081
The server, the computer waiting to respond.

17
00:00:57,081 --> 00:01:00,013
And the network, the roads connecting everything.

18
00:01:00,013 --> 00:01:02,228
And no, the internet isn't the cloud.

19
00:01:02,228 --> 00:01:06,117
The cloud is just someone else's computer wearing a fancy jacket.

20
00:01:07,042 --> 00:01:08,720
A browser is a translator.

21
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:10,722
Humans see a beautiful website.

22
00:01:10,722 --> 00:01:13,433
The browser sees HTML, CSS and JavaScript.

23
00:01:13,433 --> 00:01:18,792
Its engine, Blink, WebKit or Gecko, takes raw code and turns it into an experience.

24
00:01:19,617 --> 00:01:21,580
Think of a website like property.

25
00:01:21,580 --> 00:01:27,768
The domain is the signpost, a human-friendly address, so you never have to remember a string of numbers.

26
00:01:27,768 --> 00:01:31,337
Hosting is the plot and the building, where your files live.

27
00:01:31,337 --> 00:01:33,717
And the website is the furniture inside.

28
00:01:34,692 --> 00:01:36,482
Hosting comes in three flavours.

29
00:01:36,482 --> 00:01:40,008
Shared hosting is an apartment building, great for small sites.

30
00:01:40,008 --> 00:01:43,308
A VPS is a townhouse, a private slice of a powerful server.

31
00:01:43,308 --> 00:01:47,113
Cloud hosting is a limitless hotel, built for apps and high traffic.

32
00:01:47,113 --> 00:01:51,142
Control the hosting, and you become the ecosystem, not just the builder.

33
00:01:52,117 --> 00:01:54,255
Every webpage stands on three layers.

34
00:01:54,255 --> 00:01:58,358
HTML is the skeleton, deciding what is a heading, an image or a button.

35
00:01:58,358 --> 00:02:01,998
CSS is the interior design: colours, spacing, fonts and layout.

36
00:02:01,998 --> 00:02:03,963
And JavaScript is the electricity.

37
00:02:03,963 --> 00:02:06,217
Without it, a website is just a poster.

38
00:02:06,825 --> 00:02:07,944
Chapter two.

39
00:02:07,944 --> 00:02:10,742
The modern front-end universe.

40
00:02:11,267 --> 00:02:13,570
The web has evolved in three eras.

41
00:02:13,570 --> 00:02:13,977
Web 1.

42
00:02:13,977 --> 00:02:16,212
0 was static, a digital brochure.

43
00:02:16,212 --> 00:02:16,618
Web 2.

44
00:02:16,618 --> 00:02:19,735
0 became interactive: log in, upload, comment.

45
00:02:19,735 --> 00:02:20,142
Web 3.

46
00:02:20,142 --> 00:02:23,800
0 is intelligent, where the website becomes a partner.

47
00:02:24,550 --> 00:02:26,892
Modern websites aren't painted page by page.

48
00:02:26,892 --> 00:02:29,714
They're assembled like LEGO from reusable components.

49
00:02:29,714 --> 00:02:35,517
Instead of rebuilding the whole spaceship, you build an engine, a cockpit and wings, then snap them together.

50
00:02:36,317 --> 00:02:40,461
React, created by Meta, is the engine that builds interfaces from components.

51
00:02:40,461 --> 00:02:45,304
Think of a streaming app: profiles, a video player, recommendations, each one a component.

52
00:02:45,304 --> 00:02:46,272
Without it, chaos.

53
00:02:46,272 --> 00:02:47,080
With it, order.

54
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:48,641
So don't say, make a website.

55
00:02:48,641 --> 00:02:50,417
Ask for a React component system.

56
00:02:51,142 --> 00:02:52,382
React is the engine.

57
00:02:52,382 --> 00:02:52,692
Next.

58
00:02:52,692 --> 00:02:57,712
js is the complete vehicle, adding routing, performance, SEO and server features.

59
00:02:57,712 --> 00:02:59,758
Together, a production-ready app.

60
00:03:00,408 --> 00:03:05,803
TypeScript is the safety net: JavaScript says trust me, TypeScript says let's check first.

61
00:03:05,803 --> 00:03:08,502
Vue is the approachable alternative to React.

62
00:03:08,502 --> 00:03:12,158
And Tailwind is the speed stylist, which AI generates easily.

63
00:03:12,958 --> 00:03:15,877
A design system is where designers and developers meet.

64
00:03:15,877 --> 00:03:17,521
Without one, AI produces chaos.

65
00:03:17,521 --> 00:03:19,962
With one, it speaks in mathematical precision.

66
00:03:19,962 --> 00:03:26,275
Instead of make it look nice, say: use our design system, with rounded cards, 16 pixel spacing, and consistent buttons.

67
00:03:27,175 --> 00:03:29,947
Put it together and you have the modern stack.

68
00:03:29,947 --> 00:03:31,513
The stage, your front end.

69
00:03:31,513 --> 00:03:33,020
The logic, your back end.

70
00:03:33,020 --> 00:03:34,587
The memory, your database.

71
00:03:34,587 --> 00:03:36,575
And the home, where it all lives.

72
00:03:36,575 --> 00:03:42,058
When someone asks for a full-stack developer, this is the architecture they want commanded.

73
00:03:42,983 --> 00:03:44,116
Now you can translate.

74
00:03:44,116 --> 00:03:46,894
A React component is a reusable visual building block.

75
00:03:46,894 --> 00:03:50,342
Responsive design means it adapts across phone, tablet and desktop.

76
00:03:50,342 --> 00:03:53,121
A component library is a toolbox of ready-made pieces.

77
00:03:53,121 --> 00:03:57,083
And a SaaS application is software people access online, like Canva or Slack.

78
00:03:57,833 --> 00:04:02,718
You now speak the language of the internet, browsers, the modern stack and component systems.

79
00:04:02,718 --> 00:04:07,233
Next up, chapter three: Motion and Magic, where websites become cinematic experiences.

80
00:04:07,658 --> 00:04:08,501
Chapter three.

81
00:04:08,501 --> 00:04:09,526
Motion and magic.

82
00:04:09,526 --> 00:04:11,575
Turning websites into experiences.

83
00:04:12,075 --> 00:04:14,859
A website is no longer just a collection of pages.

84
00:04:14,859 --> 00:04:19,704
Modern websites behave like films, games, interactive installations and digital worlds.

85
00:04:19,704 --> 00:04:21,151
Movement guides attention.

86
00:04:21,151 --> 00:04:22,544
Movement creates emotion.

87
00:04:22,544 --> 00:04:23,825
Movement tells a story.

88
00:04:24,675 --> 00:04:26,933
Before the tools, learn the vocabulary.

89
00:04:26,933 --> 00:04:29,481
A transition is a change between two states.

90
00:04:29,481 --> 00:04:32,898
A hover is an interaction when a cursor lands on something.

91
00:04:32,898 --> 00:04:37,125
Micro-interactions are tiny animations that make an interface feel alive.

92
00:04:37,125 --> 00:04:39,558
And easing is the personality of movement.

93
00:04:40,433 --> 00:04:42,802
Easing is the personality of movement.

94
00:04:42,802 --> 00:04:44,361
Linear is constant speed.

95
00:04:44,361 --> 00:04:45,047
Mechanical.

96
00:04:45,047 --> 00:04:47,479
Ease-in starts slowly, building energy.

97
00:04:47,479 --> 00:04:49,163
Ease-out slows down gently.

98
00:04:49,163 --> 00:04:49,661
Natural.

99
00:04:49,661 --> 00:04:52,966
And spring feels physical, like an object has weight.

100
00:04:53,866 --> 00:04:58,212
GSAP, the GreenSock Animation Platform, is the Hollywood camera crew of websites.

101
00:04:58,212 --> 00:05:02,344
It controls position, scale, rotation, opacity, colour, timing and sequences.

102
00:05:02,344 --> 00:05:03,900
One hero section, five moves.

103
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:04,865
The logo fades in.

104
00:05:04,865 --> 00:05:05,670
Text slides up.

105
00:05:05,670 --> 00:05:06,958
The image zooms forward.

106
00:05:06,958 --> 00:05:07,870
Particles appear.

107
00:05:07,870 --> 00:05:08,835
The button pulses.

108
00:05:08,835 --> 00:05:09,533
One timeline.

109
00:05:10,508 --> 00:05:10,854
Anime.

110
00:05:10,854 --> 00:05:17,545
js is lighter than GSAP, a beautifully animated short film, perfect for logos, menus and cards appearing one by one.

111
00:05:17,545 --> 00:05:19,450
Framer Motion is built for React.

112
00:05:19,450 --> 00:05:22,391
A card enters from below, fading in and scaling up.

113
00:05:22,391 --> 00:05:25,391
Perfect for page transitions, modals and dashboards.

114
00:05:26,341 --> 00:05:29,882
Lottie exports After Effects animations as JSON files.

115
00:05:29,882 --> 00:05:32,964
Perfect for mascots, loading screens and icons.

116
00:05:32,964 --> 00:05:34,865
It says: play this animation.

117
00:05:34,865 --> 00:05:36,897
Rive is its interactive cousin.

118
00:05:36,897 --> 00:05:38,799
It says: respond to the user.

119
00:05:38,799 --> 00:05:41,225
A character reacts when you click it.

120
00:05:42,125 --> 00:05:44,916
Smooth scrolling makes a website feel expensive.

121
00:05:44,916 --> 00:05:46,311
Default scrolling jumps.

122
00:05:46,311 --> 00:05:51,255
Premium sites glide, with tools like Lenis, Locomotive Scroll and GSAP ScrollTrigger.

123
00:05:51,255 --> 00:05:52,417
Parallax adds depth.

124
00:05:52,417 --> 00:05:53,930
The background moves slow.

125
00:05:53,930 --> 00:05:55,441
The foreground moves fast.

126
00:05:56,391 --> 00:05:59,065
ScrollTrigger connects animation to scrolling.

127
00:05:59,065 --> 00:06:01,041
At zero percent, the hero appears.

128
00:06:01,041 --> 00:06:02,960
At twenty-five, the text reveals.

129
00:06:02,960 --> 00:06:04,704
At fifty, the product rotates.

130
00:06:04,704 --> 00:06:07,435
At seventy-five, the feature section activates.

131
00:06:07,435 --> 00:06:09,935
At one hundred, the call to action appears.

132
00:06:09,935 --> 00:06:12,841
This is how many award-winning websites are built.

133
00:06:13,816 --> 00:06:15,604
There are three levels of animation.

134
00:06:15,604 --> 00:06:19,625
Level one is functional: useful movement, like buttons, menus and loading states.

135
00:06:19,625 --> 00:06:24,094
Level two is premium, adding personality: smooth transitions, hover effects, page reveals.

136
00:06:24,094 --> 00:06:27,916
Level three is cinematic: storytelling scroll, 3D scenes, interactive worlds.

137
00:06:28,766 --> 00:06:30,515
Creative director translation.

138
00:06:30,515 --> 00:06:31,623
GSAP ScrollTrigger?

139
00:06:31,623 --> 00:06:34,421
Make scrolling behave like a cinematic sequence.

140
00:06:34,421 --> 00:06:35,237
Framer Motion?

141
00:06:35,237 --> 00:06:37,277
Add beautiful React-based movement.

142
00:06:37,277 --> 00:06:38,385
Micro-interactions?

143
00:06:38,385 --> 00:06:41,300
Add tiny moments that make the product feel alive.

144
00:06:42,125 --> 00:06:43,399
The NagaVision rule.

145
00:06:43,399 --> 00:06:44,865
A good website informs.

146
00:06:44,865 --> 00:06:46,457
A great website performs.

147
00:06:46,457 --> 00:06:52,893
The future belongs to experiences that combine design, motion, sound, interaction, A I, 3D and story.

148
00:06:52,893 --> 00:06:55,441
Next up, Chapter 4: the third dimension.
